winemac-qt5-opengl.patch - Gamify patch over CrossOver 25.1.0 Wine (dlls/winemac.drv), LGPL-2.1-or-later.
Found with Worms W.M.D (Steam 327030, 32-bit Qt5 + OpenGL); details in docs/worms-opengl.md.
 1. OpenGL on message-only windows: set_pixel_format() creates Mac data (a Cocoa window that is
    never shown) for a window whose parent is HWND_MESSAGE (Qt 5's "QtOpenGLDummyWindow",
    QOffscreenSurface). Before, SetPixelFormat failed ("DC for window of other process").
 2. Mac Driver option ForceOpenGLCoreContext: a legacy (< 3.0) context request gets the newest core
    profile (4.1) plus a default VAO that stands in for VAO 0. macOS has no compatibility profile
    above 2.1; Windows drivers return 4.x compatibility, which games with GLSL 330 rely on.
 3. Mac Driver option OpenGLAttribDeclarationOrder: before glLinkProgram, bind the vertex shader's
    inputs in declaration order (Windows driver behaviour; Apple sorts them by name).
 2 and 3 are off by default, on for "Worms W.M.D.exe"; HKCU\Software\Wine[\AppDefaults\<exe>]\Mac Driver
 overrides them ("y"/"n").
Apply: patch -p1 -d upstream/crossover-sources-25.1.0/sources/wine < src/patches/winemac-qt5-opengl.patch

